    "cold_open": "There is an old lighthouse near the sea, and sometimes its light turns on at night.",
    "question": "Why does it glow when no one is there, even during the worst storms?",
    "journey": "A boy from the village often watches the light flicker through the storm. He walks to the lighthouse on moonlit nights, drawn by the glow. Inside, he finds the old keeper's desk, untouched, with a journal and a faded photograph. The pages whisper of storms, of duty, of a man who once kept the light burning for ships lost at sea.",
    "discovery": "One night, the boy finds the lamp lit without a match. The journal speaks of a promise made to the sea, a vow to light the lamp until the storm passed. The boy realizes the keeper's spirit still lingers, bound to his duty.",
